   "id": 631860,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>The functions describing the time that baseballs stayed in the air, in seconds, that four baseball players hit are below.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><span data-math=\"f(t)=(-16t-1)(t-5)\">f(t)=(-16t-1)(t-5)</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"g(t)=(-16t-1)(t-10)\">g(t)=(-16t-1)(t-10)</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"h(t)=(t-7)(-16t-1)\">h(t)=(t-7)(-16t-1)</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"p(t)=(-8t-1)(2t-5)\">p(t)=(-8t-1)(2t-5)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Which function represents the ball that stayed in the air the longest?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1223050,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"p(t)=(-8t-1)(2t-5)\">p(t)=(-8t-1)(2t-5)</span>"
